@firstof9 as per our other discussion, I did create a proof-of-concept tracking a "last known brightness." I understand the reasons why we wouldn't want to do that, but I did want to put this solution out there (and maybe for others in this situation). I'm using this locally and it's a 10x better experience in the UI. The UI always reflects reality, and I can turn on a light, see what it's brightness is, and make adjustments, etc, and everything works as expected and matches the UI.

The only downside is that if the value that HA is tracking gets _off_, then when you turn on the dimmer via HA, it could set it to the wrong last known brightness. The chances for that aren't very high, and I personally find this a better solution, because even if it is the wrong value, at least the UI is matching the reality of this, and it will show the actual value that the lights have been set to.

Anyway, I made a PoC PR against this branch (to just see the additional changes) here: https://github.com/firstof9/core/pull/1
